WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Local M5 login: existing OIDC session expired; the Hub requires a new login.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Admin overview after real Dex OIDC login: two connected mTLS Workers and retained
operation history.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Both Workers connected: Agent version m5, last heartbeat and actual transport state.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Tenant A Owner overview exposes only Tenant A applications and history.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Owner submits video-pricing v1 to the provisioned Worker A through the typed HTML
form.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
The accepted deployment is pending; success waits for actual Kubernetes rollout.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Browser release of v2-good and replicas=2 is queued as revision 2.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
v2-good READY, revision 2 and replicas=2 after actual Operator drift repair;
persistent history survived Hub recreation.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Release v2-broken is revision 3; the previous successful revision remains 2.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Worker B Agent is deliberately paused: DISCONNECTED preserves its last heartbeat;
the local workload remains available.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
The same Worker B Agent reconnects over mTLS with a fresh heartbeat.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
v2-broken failed with real ProgressDeadlineExceeded; revision 2 stays last
successful and the request ID is retained.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Rollback confirmation selects successful revision 1 and will create a new revision;
it does not erase revision 3.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Confirmed rollback is accepted as revision 4, with prior failure history preserved.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Rollback revision 4 is READY with v1; revision 3 remains FAILED and the original CR
UID is unchanged.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Applications filters show only the authorized Tenant A and Worker A, including
revision 4 recovery.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Tenant A Owner is denied when opening the known Tenant B application; no foreign
details are exposed.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Viewer sees actual Ready/Conditions and preserved releases, with no deployment,
rollback or delete controls.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Viewer is denied access to platform-wide Prometheus metrics by server-side
authorization.
